  "title": "Unified title",
  "summary": "Team RAS in the 11th ABAW Competition presents a multimodal approach for recognizing ambivalence and hesitancy, combining linguistic, acoustic, facial, and scene features using text-centered fusion models. The Text Residual Fusion model achieves high performance across different subsets of the BAH corpus.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Text Residual Fusion model achieves an average Macro F1-score (MF1) of 75.14% across the Development and Public Test subsets.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "On the Private Test subset, it reaches an MF1 of 78.24%, outperforming the text model by 4.03%.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Text Residual Fusion model combines text as the anchor modality and applies gated residual adjustments based on other modalities.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
